Consider we have 5 services to run to run our overall application so earlier we run docker run for each service and make it up then once all 5 service up our complete app will ru, instead we can add all the application in docker compose and if we up dockercompose file our app will be up, intead of managing each services.

Here sample docker compose configuration file:
Start with services, then mention all the services name ie vote, result etc that is our given name, then on each service metion image: and mention the image name else use build: ./vote here vote is folder name , inside the folder need to kep Dockerfile, So when you run the docker compose up it will build the image from dockerfile and run the container.Then if the container has port need to metion that and its list and if network created need to mention the network on same indent as parent services and keep the all network name in object, then on each service need to metion the networks: here if the service has multiple network can mention in list else we can keep one in list. To add environment variablke need to use envieonment ket on service and mention all environment in key value pair on environment object . For volume , need to do like network first create volume object on same indent as services and mention the host mount name as object then on service need to mention on volume object and mention the full path ie - data-db:/var/lib/postgresql/data
services:
  vote:
    image:vote
    or
    build:./vote
    ports:
      -"5001:80"
    networks:["fornt-end","back-end"]
  redis:
    image:redis
    ports:
      -"5002:80"
    networks:["back-end"]
  worker:
    image:worker
    ports:
      -"5003:80"
    networks:["back-end"]
  postgres:
    image:postgres
    ports:
      -"5004:5432"
    networks:["back-end"]
    volumes:
      - data-db:/var/lib/postgresql/data
    environment:
      Postgres_User: postgres
      Postgres_Password: password

  result:
    image:result
    ports:
      -"5005:80"
    networks:["fornt-end","back-end"]
networks:
  fornt-end:
  back-end:
volumes:
  data-db:

Command to create a network
docker network create nm_name
Command to list the available network
docker newtwok ls
command to remove the network:
docker network rm id

Command to run the dockercompose file:
docker compose -f configuration.yml up
Command to stop the docker compose
docker compose -f configuration.yml down

